      <scopecontent id="aspace_ac3ebd04e44dd0c8902e8dfba56947a6">
         <head>Scope and Contents</head>
         <p>The Carlo Tommaso Maillard de Tournon Collection consists of correspondence, a journal, and printed material which document Tournon's legation to the Sino-Manchu empire (1705-1710). Correspondence includes letters in Italian, Latin, French, and Spanish by Tournon, members of his staff, and associates. The collection also includes later letters (1711-1726) by missionaries in China. A journal from 1705 to 1710 contains entries made by Giovanni Borghese, Tournon's personal physician. At the end of the collection there is twentieth century printed material concerning Tournon and the significance of his mission to China.</p>
         <p>The collection was transferred from the Miscellaneous Manuscripts Collection (MS 352) in 1987.</p>
      </scopecontent>
